 JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed in `README.md`.

+## Authentication
+
+Send `Authorization: Bearer <key>` with every request. Missing or unknown
+keys return 401 (`unauthorized`). Valid keys with insufficient permissions
+return 403 (`forbidden`).
+
+- Viewers can use GET routes except `GET /audit`.
+- Cooks can also use `POST /recipes/:id/cook`, `POST /batches/:id/waste`,
+  `POST /temperatures`, and `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- Managers can use every route.
+
+## Routes
+
+`GET /audit` returns an array of successful write requests, newest first.
+Each entry contains `time` (ISO 8601 UTC), `name` (the key name), `method`,
+`path` (without the query string), and `status` (the HTTP status code).
+This route requires a manager key.
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
